@startuml LostUpdatePreventionClockPush
title Lost Update Prevention via HLC Clock Push\n(Snapshot Isolation, no Raft / no replication)

actor "Bob\n(slow client)\nclock starts (1000,0)" as Bob
actor "Alice\n(fast client)\nclock starts (2000,0)" as Alice

box "Cluster (3 nodes, distinct roles)" #FAFAFA
  participant "C_b\nbob's coordinator" as Cb
  participant "C_a\nalice's coordinator" as Ca
  participant "K\nkey owner\n(sharedKey)" as K
end box

note over Bob, K
  Routing constraint: C_b != C_a != K (three distinct nodes).
  Status-check RPC is the **only** path by which alice's HLC
  can reach bob's coordinator.
end note

== 1. Begin transactions ==

Bob -> Cb : BeginTxn(bobTxn, clientTime=(1000,0))
activate Cb
note right of Cb : merge -> C_b.hlc = (1000,1)\nstore TxnRecord{PENDING, readTs=(1000,1)}
Cb --> Bob : success, propagated=(1000,1)
deactivate Cb

Alice -> Ca : BeginTxn(aliceTxn, clientTime=(2000,0))
activate Ca
note right of Ca : merge -> C_a.hlc = (2000,1)\n**alice.snapshot = (2000,1)**
Ca --> Alice : success, propagated=(2000,1)
deactivate Ca

== 2. Bob writes intent at K ==

Bob -> K : Write(key, "100", readTs=(1000,1), clientTime=(1000,*))
activate K
note right of K : merge -> K.hlc ~ (1000,*)\nput intent @ (1000,*)
K --> Bob : success
deactivate K
note over Cb : C_b.hlc is **still ~ (1000,*)**\nalice's clock has not reached it yet

== 3. Alice's read - the clock-push pivot ==

Alice -> K : Read(key, readTs=(2000,1), clientTime=(2000,*))
activate K
note right of K #FFE0B2
  **PUSH HOP 1:**
  merge -> K.hlc jumps to (2000,*)
  finds bob's pending intent
end note
K -> Cb : GetTransactionStatus(bobTxn, clientTime=K.hlc.now())
activate Cb
note right of Cb #FFCDD2
  **PUSH HOP 2 - the key event:**
  merge -> C_b.hlc jumps from
  (1000,*) to (2000,*)
end note
Cb --> K : status=PENDING, propagated=(2000,*)
deactivate Cb
note right of K
  SI policy: ignore pending intent
  -> read committed @ readTs
  -> no committed version
end note
K --> Alice : not found
deactivate K

== 4. Bob commits - at a now-pushed-up timestamp ==

Bob -> Cb : Commit(bobTxn, clientTime=(1000,*))
activate Cb
note right of Cb #C8E6C9
  commitTs = hybridClock.now()
  C_b.hlc was pushed -> (2000,*)
  -> **commitTs > alice.snapshot** OK
end note
Cb -->> K : Resolve(bobTxn, commitTs) [fire-and-forget]
Cb --> Bob : success, commitTs=(2000,*)
deactivate Cb

K -> K : move intent -> committedStore @ commitTs
note right of K : test waits here via\nsteps.await(hasCommittedValue)

== 5. Alice's write rejected - lost update prevented ==

Alice -> K : Write(key, "200", readTs=(2000,1))
activate K
note right of K #FFCDD2
  hasCommittedVersionAfter(key, readTs)?
  committed @ (2000,*) > readTs (2000,1)
  -> **STALE**
end note
K --> Alice : error "Conflicting committed transaction"
deactivate K

== Post-run assertions ==

note over Bob, K
  * **bobSeed (1000,0) < aliceSnapshot**     - BEFORE: bob starts below the snapshot
  * **bobCommitTs > aliceSnapshot**          - AFTER:  the push lifted him above it
  * **alice.write -> "Conflicting committed transaction"**
                                             - OUTCOME: lost update prevented (SI rule 2)
  The before/after pair makes the push falsifiable; absent it bob commits at ~1000
  and alice's blind write would silently overwrite him.
end note

@enduml
